al-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Connecticut enters the presidential race as a Democratic-leaning state with no incumbent on the ballot. The estimate rests on the state's partisan fundamentals, which favor the Democratic nominee by roughly eight points. No public general-election polls or expert ratings are yet available for this contest, so the projection carries wide uncertainty.\n\nRecent coverage has centered on Democratic activity in the state, including Senator Chris Murphy's national profile and 2028 primary positioning, but nothing indicates a change in Connecticut's presidential partisanship. The state has been a dependable Democratic performer in recent cycles, and the absence of an incumbent does not alter that underlying lean. The Republican nominee would need a substantial national environment shift to put the state in play. Until polling emerges, the race is best described as a Democratic lean with meaningful but not extreme uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8243, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.781, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7754, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7619, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7738, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7843, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7768, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7843, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7811, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7718, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7751, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7661, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7723, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7668, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7815, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.7783, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.7655, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-